<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_IrqitTarruq.xml                      RimMandrake — CRACKEDLANDS_RULED_CONTENT_1

  Two of the Cracked Lands' five ruled new natives, both invented (no donor def).
  Bible: design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/cracked_lands_bedazzle_cast_2026-09-28.md
  §"RM_Irqit — the mudflat breeder" and §"RM_Tarruq — the voice". Roster wiring
  (wildAnimals rows, commonality) is a LATER pass over the shared roster/patch
  files, per this item's own file-collision split — not done here.

  ═══════════════════════════ RM_Irqit — the mudflat breeder ═══════════════════════════

  Bible stats sketch, taken as-is: baseBodySize ~0.12, herd-spawning, MoveSpeed
  ~4.5, wildness 1.0, no manhunter, trivial combat stats, tiny meat yield (left to
  the engine's own bodySize->meat computation rather than an override — 0.12 is
  already the smallest body in this file by a wide margin).

  The bible's lifecycle mechanism ("spawned as a cohort on the flood
  component's soaked-cell list at recede... at dry-out the cohort dies where it
  stands") is Source/RM_MapComponent_RecedeAftermath.cs
  (CRACKEDLANDS_GPT_ENRICHMENT_1 §5): a bounded cohort on the wetted cells,
  each tagged RM_IrqitFloodBorn, killed at the dry so the corpses are the
  windrows. This def stays an ordinary small animal, so it can still be spawned
  by vanilla means (quicktest, `jawa/spawn_thing`) without erroring.

  LIFECYCLE SHAPE CHOSEN HERE: a single lifeStage (AnimalAdult, minAge 0) — no
  baby/juvenile split, matching this biome's OWN precedent for a creature that is
  born ready to act (RM_Nizzek, Stillsand/RM_Drazzik.xml, same single-stage
  shape for a newborn that hatches "already hostile"). The irqit's version of
  that idiom is "born already able to scramble and breed once" — a baby/juvenile
  stage would imply a growth arc the bible explicitly denies ("breeds exactly
  once... dies as the mud stiffens").

  lifeExpectancy: no sub-1-year precedent exists anywhere in this codebase
  (checked: `grep -rn "lifeExpectancy>0\." src/RimMandrake src/RimUtinni` — zero
  hits) so there is no convention to match exactly. Chosen here: 0.05 (~18
  days), inside the bible's own "a few days to weeks" frame and short enough to
  read as a flood-week creature if the vanilla aging curve is ever left to run
  it unassisted. The mechanics item's fast lifecycle clock is expected to
  override/drive the real cohort timing regardless — this field is a plausible
  fallback, not the actual clock.

  ═══════════════════════════════ RM_Tarruq — the voice ═══════════════════════════════

  Bible stats sketch, taken as-is: baseBodySize ~0.45, MoveSpeed ~4.8, agile, shy
  (high wildness, no manhunter — "it answers threat by going vertical"), modest
  predator diet (crack-life/irqit stragglers/eggs — foodType CarnivoreAnimal).
  Year-round resident (standard baby/juvenile/adult lifeStageAges, no seasonal
  gimmick). ROSTER COMMONALITY (not wired here, for the wiring pass): bible says
  ~0.1-0.15.

  Body: Monkey — a lean climbing quadruped shape reads closest to "long-limbed
  climber built for the vertical dark" of the bodies already in use in this
  codebase (grep of `<body>` across src/RimMandrake); no dedicated climber body
  exists to match more precisely.

  The bible's ambient-call/silence mechanism: the GATE is built
  (Source/RM_TarruqHushPatch.cs skips the idle call while the flood component's
  TarruqSilenced is true, i.e. from the herald's third beat to the recede). The
  CALL is vanilla Pawn_Muffalo_Call on the juvenile and adult stages (the long
  low lowing is the closest vanilla grain to "long low tones the canyon carries";
  owner 2026-10-03: vanilla audio ships as final, CRACKEDLANDS_FIVE_BEATS_AUDIO_1).

  ═════════════════════════════════════ ART ═════════════════════════════════════

  Both are covered in this sitting's art commission
  (infrastructure/artpipe/art_lists/cracked_lands_bedazzle_cast.csv — checked,
  rows present for RM_Irqit and RM_Tarruq) so no fill_queue.py job is filed here.
  Until that art lands, both ship with a LOUD vanilla placeholder texPath, same
  posture as this codebase's other invented (donor-less) creatures
  (Stillsand/RM_Drazzik.xml's RM_Nizzek uses vanilla Chicken; RM_Guzzka points at
  its own not-yet-populated folder). Irqit points at vanilla Rat (small,
  ground-hugging, plausible silhouette for a palm-sized scrambler); Tarruq points
  at vanilla Monkey (climbing quadruped, plausible silhouette for a lean
  crack-dweller).
-->
<Defs>

  <!-- ══════════════════════ RM_Irqit — the mudflat breeder ══════════════════════ -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Irqit</defName>
    <label>irqit</label>
    <description>Palm-sized and soft-bodied, glossy wet skin over a quick paddling scramble — the irqit exists as eggs in the dry clay for years, waiting. When the flood recedes, every soaked cell turns into a nursery: a sudden carpet of small frantic life between the roar and the dry. Each one breeds exactly once, lays into the wet clay, and dies as the mud stiffens. It is a living calendar of the flood, gone as completely as it arrived.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>4.5</MoveSpeed>
      <MarketValue>3</MarketValue>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>10</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>60</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <FilthRate>1</FilthRate>
      <Wildness>1.0</Wildness>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>nip</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>1.5</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Teeth</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <chanceFactor>0.2</chanceFactor>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <race>
      <body>QuadrupedAnimalWithPawsAndTail</body>
      <predator>false</predator>
      <herdAnimal>true</herdAnimal>
      <baseBodySize>0.12</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>0.15</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>0.2</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>OmnivoreRoughAnimal</foodType>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>0</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <manhunterOnTameFailChance>0</manhunterOnTameFailChance>
      <!-- See header: no sub-1-year precedent exists in this codebase; chosen to
           sit inside the bible's "days to weeks" frame as a plausible fallback,
           not the real cohort clock (that is CRACKEDLANDS_MECHANICS_BUILD_1's). -->
      <lifeExpectancy>0.05</lifeExpectancy>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
    </race>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalCommon</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RM_Irqit</defName>
    <label>irqit</label>
    <race>RM_Irqit</race>
    <combatPower>2</combatPower>
    <canArriveManhunter>false</canArriveManhunter>
    <!-- "Herd-spawning" / "a sudden carpet" — a high wildGroupSize on an ordinary
         PawnKindDef, same idiom this codebase already uses for a swarm creature
         (Miasma/RM_Karrimeth's 40~90). The real cohort-on-recede spawn is the
         mechanics item's; this is what a vanilla/manual spawn call produces
         until that lands. -->
    <wildGroupSize>15~40</wildGroupSize>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0.05</ecoSystemWeight>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <!-- TEMP PLACEHOLDER: vanilla Rat's own body art. No donor def exists
               (invented per the bible); real art is queued in
               cracked_lands_bedazzle_cast.csv (row present, checked this pass). -->
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Rat/Rat</texPath>
          <color>(150,140,110)</color>
          <drawSize>0.5</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
        <dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Rat/Dessicated_Rat</texPath>
          <drawSize>0.5</drawSize>
        </dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════ RM_Tarruq — the voice ══════════════════════════════ -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Tarruq</defName>
    <label>tarruq</label>
    <description>A lean, long-limbed climber built for the vertical dark of the crack network — grip-padded feet, a deep resonating throat-chamber that carries its low territorial calls for hundreds of meters, each animal answering its neighbors down the line. On an ordinary day the Cracked Lands' soundscape is wind, then tarruq, then wind. It goes silent and climbs when the cracks begin to fill — a Farmer trusts that hush as the biome's second warning, before even the chimes.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>4.8</MoveSpeed>
      <MarketValue>60</MarketValue>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>5</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>70</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <FilthRate>2</FilthRate>
      <Wildness>0.9</Wildness>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>left claw</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>7</power>
        <cooldownTime>1.7</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>LeftHand</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>right claw</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>7</power>
        <cooldownTime>1.7</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>RightHand</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
      <li>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>6</power>
        <cooldownTime>1.8</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Teeth</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <chanceFactor>0.4</chanceFactor>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <race>
      <body>Monkey</body>
      <predator>true</predator>
      <herdAnimal>false</herdAnimal>
      <baseBodySize>0.45</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>0.5</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>0.3</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>CarnivoreAnimal, OvivoreAnimal</foodType>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <!-- Shy, not aggressive — "it answers threat by going vertical". -->
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>0</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <manhunterOnTameFailChance>0.02</manhunterOnTameFailChance>
      <gestationPeriodDays>14</gestationPeriodDays>
      <lifeExpectancy>11</lifeExpectancy>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.2</minAge>
          <soundCall>Pawn_Muffalo_Call</soundCall>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.4</minAge>
          <soundCall>Pawn_Muffalo_Call</soundCall>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
    </race>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalCommon</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RM_Tarruq</defName>
    <label>tarruq</label>
    <race>RM_Tarruq</race>
    <combatPower>55</combatPower>
    <!-- Shy, low-commonality resident — roster commonality (~0.1-0.15 per the
         bible) is the wiring pass's, not this def's; wildGroupSize here just
         keeps it from reading as a herd animal. -->
    <wildGroupSize>1~2</wildGroupSize>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0.2</ecoSystemWeight>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <label>tarruq kit</label>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <!-- TEMP PLACEHOLDER: vanilla Monkey's own body art. No donor def
               exists (invented per the bible); real art is queued in
               cracked_lands_bedazzle_cast.csv (row present, checked this pass). -->
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Monkey/Monkey</texPath>
          <color>(140,130,115)</color>
          <drawSize>0.7</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
        <dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Monkey/Dessicated_Monkey</texPath>
          <drawSize>0.7</drawSize>
        </dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Monkey/Monkey</texPath>
          <color>(140,130,115)</color>
          <drawSize>1.0</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
        <dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Monkey/Dessicated_Monkey</texPath>
          <drawSize>1.0</drawSize>
        </dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Monkey/Monkey</texPath>
          <color>(140,130,115)</color>
          <drawSize>1.3</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
        <dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Monkey/Dessicated_Monkey</texPath>
          <drawSize>1.3</drawSize>
        </dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

</Defs>
